<v Speaker 1>while Van Lunen had decided to try and outthink the meta game with a base white life gain and milling deck that featured Rites of Flourishing together with Howling Mines to eventually deck the opponent. One game up, the Russian watched. Van Lunen established an impenetrable life total thanks to Martyr of Sands and a very short clock courtesy of a full set of Rites of Flourishing and double Howling Mine. This meant both players were drawing 7 cards a turn. Isn't magic great? So</v>

